To manage dynamic load and failures, the Java service uses retry logic and backoff strategies to gracefully degrade if the external API becomes unreliable. The service also utilizes circuit breakers to prevent cascading failures in case of a failure. The C-based module also implements similar techniques for handling failures and managing resource utilization under varying workloads.

