['Here is a code block that implements the data processing framework described in the task:
```java
import org.apache.spark.sql.*;
import org.apache.spark.api.java.JavaSparkContext;
import org.apache.spark.api.java.JavaRDD;
import java.util.List;
import java.util.HashMap;
import java.util.Map;

public class DataProcessingFramework {
    private static final Logger LOGGER = LoggerFactory.getLogger(DataProcessingFramework.class);
    private JavaSparkContext sparkContext;
    private Map<String, Function<DataFrame, DataFrame>> dataTransformations = new HashMap<>();

    public void initialize(JavaSparkContext sparkContext) {
        this.sparkContext = sparkContext;
    }

    public void registerDataTransformation(String name, Function<DataFrame, DataFrame> transformation) {
        dataTransformations.put(name, transformation);
    }

    public DataFrame transform(DataFrame inputDF, String... transformations) {
        for (String transformation : transformations) {
            if (dataTransformations.containsKey(transformation)) {
                inputDF = dataTransformations.get(transformation).apply(inputDF);
            } else {
                LOGGER.warn("Transformation {} is not registered", transformation);
            }
        }
        return inputDF;
    }

    public void run() throws Exception {
        JavaRDD<String> lines = sparkContext.textFile("external-data-ingestion-pipeline").cache();
        DataFrame inputDF = sparkContext.read().json(lines).cache();
        List<String> transformations = new ArrayList<>();

        // Get the list of registered data transformations from configuration files
        String[] transformationNames = {"transformation1", "transformation2", "transformation3"};
        for (String transformationName : transformationNames) {
            if (dataTransformations.containsKey(transformationName)) {
                transformations.add(transformationName);
            } else {
                LOGGER.warn("Transformation {} is not registered", transformationName);
            }
        }

        // Execute the data transformations in parallel using Spark
        DataFrame outputDF = transform(inputDF, transformations.toArray(new String[transformations.size()]));

        // Save the transformed data to an external storage system
        outputDF.write().mode("overwrite").option("header", "true").csv("transformed-data");
    }
}
```
The framework consists of a `DataProcessingFramework` class that is responsible for managing the data transformations, caching, and saving the transformed data to an external storage system. The `initialize` method initializes the Spark context and sets up the list of registered data transformations. The `registerDataTransformation` method allows the user to register custom data transformations using a function from Apache Spark's API. The `transform` method applies the registered data transformations in parallel on the input DataFrame using Spark, returning the transformed DataFrame. Finally, the `run` method reads the input data from an external storage system using Spark, applies the registered data transformations, and saves the transformed data to another external storage system.']

