### UUID Generation Mechanism

To generate unique UUIDs for resources, we will use a combination of a distributed counter and a hash function. The distributed counter will be used to assign a sequence number to each request, which will then be hashed using the `MD5` algorithm to produce a unique identifier. This approach ensures high throughput in high-demand environments while still providing unique identifiers.
```java
import java.util.concurrent.atomic.AtomicLong;
import java.security.MessageDigest;

public class UUIDGenerator {
    private static final AtomicLong sequence = new AtomicLong();

    public String generateUUID() {
        long seq = sequence.getAndIncrement();
        byte[] hash = MessageDigest.getInstance("MD5").digest(String.valueOf(seq).getBytes());
        return bytesToHex(hash);
    }

    private static final String bytesToHex(byte[] bytes) {
        StringBuilder sb = new StringBuilder();
        for (int i = 0; i < bytes.length; i++) {
            sb.append(String.format("%02X", bytes[i]));
        }
        return sb.toString();
    }
}
```
