In this example, we use a `std::map` to keep track of the locks for each file path. We also use a `std::mutex` object instead of a raw C++ mutex to make it easier to use and manage the locks.

Note that this is just one possible way to implement thread-safe file access in C++, and there are many other approaches we could take depending on the specific requirements of our application."]

