* `init_srb_contexts_persistent()`: This function is used to handle persistent storage of SRB contexts between function calls. It creates a local copy of the SRB context array and initializes it with the provided configuration parameters. It then releases the lock on the SRB context array.

These functions can be called from different parts of the code, depending on the requirements of the application. For example, `init_srb_contexts()` can be called when the application starts up to initialize the SRB context array with the provided configuration parameters. `init_srb_contexts_wrapper()` can be used to handle concurrent access from multiple threads, while `init_srb_contexts_async()` can be used to handle asynchronous data retrieval and processing. Similarly, `init_srb_contexts_rate_limits()` can be used to handle rate limits imposed by the external API and implement throttling strategies, and `init_srb_contexts_persistent()` can be used to handle persistent storage of SRB contexts between function calls.']

