The `processPacket()` function of the `RfProcessor` class takes an RF packet as input and applies the appropriate processing pipeline to it using the `addPipeline()` and `removePipeline()` functions of the `ProcessingQueue` and `ProcessingBuffer` classes. The `processPackets()` function of the `RfProcessor` class takes a vector of RF packets as input and processes each packet in the vector using the appropriate processing pipeline.

