    try {
      BasicProperties props = new BasicProperties();
      props.builder().setHeader("sender", senderJID).build();
      amqpChannel.basicPublish("", "amqp_queue", props, payload.getBytes());
    } catch (IOException | TimeoutException e) {
      System.err.println("Error publishing message to AMQP: " + e.getMessage());
    }
  }

  private MqttClient getMQTTClient(String topic) throws MqttException {
    MqttClient mqttClient = mqttClients.get(topic);
    if (mqttClient == null) {
      mqttClient = new MqttClient("tcp://localhost:1883", "mqtt_client_" + topic);
      mqttClients.put(topic, mqttClient);
      return mqttClient;
    }
    return mqttClient;
  }

  private Channel getAMQPChannel(String queue) throws IOException, TimeoutException {
    Channel amqpChannel = amqpChannels.get(queue);
    if (amqpChannel == null) {
      ConnectionFactory factory = new ConnectionFactory();
      factory.setHost("localhost");
      Connection connection = factory.newConnection();
      amqpChannel = connection.createChannel();
      amqpChannels.put(queue, amqpChannel);
    }
    return amqpChannel;
  }

  public void shutdown() {
    // Shut down all XMPP connections and MQTT clients
    for (XMPPConnection connection : xmppConnections.values()) {
      try {
        connection.disconnect();
      } catch (SmackException | InterruptedException e) {
        System.err.println("Error disconnecting from XMPP: " + e.getMessage());
      }
    }
    for (MqttClient client : mqttClients.values()) {
      try {
        client.disconnect();
      } catch (MqttException e) {
        System.err.println("Error disconnecting from MQTT: " + e.getMessage());
      }
    }
  }
}
```

The `RealTimeMessagingApplication` class manages the connections to the messaging providers and dispatches messages between them. It contains several methods for sending and receiving messages, as well as an `initialize()` method that initializes the connection to each provider and a `shutdown()` method that disconnects from all providers when the application is shut down.

The `sendMessage(String message, String user)` method sends a message to the messaging provider for the specified user. It first checks if there is an existing XMPP connection for the user and creates one if necessary. Then it sends the message using the `XMPPConnection` instance.

The `receiveMessage(String message, String sender)` method receives a message from any of the messaging providers. It extracts the payload and sender from the JSON string and then sends the message to the appropriate messaging provider based on the sender's JID.

The `getXMPPConnection(String user)` method returns an existing XMPP connection for the specified user, or creates a new one if necessary. It uses the `XMPPConnection` class from the Smack library to connect to the messaging provider and retrieve the user's JID.

The `getMQTTClient(String topic)` method returns an existing MQTT client for the specified topic, or creates a new one if necessary. It uses the `MqttClient` class from the Paho MQTT library to connect to the messaging provider and subscribe to the topic.

The `getAMQPChannel(String queue)` method returns an existing AMQP channel for the specified queue, or creates a new one if necessary. It uses the `ConnectionFactory` class from the RabbitMQ client library to establish a connection with the messaging provider and then creates a channel for sending and receiving messages.

The `shutdown()` method disconnects from all providers when the application is shut down. It uses the `disconnect()` method of each provider to close the connection.']

