The system also includes robust retry mechanisms to detect and recover from transient failures, as well as comprehensive logging and monitoring capabilities for troubleshooting and optimization. The system is designed to handle bursty data inputs gracefully, minimizing the risk of buffer overflows and ensuring consistent throughput.

The `StreamingDataProcessor` is highly available, distributed, and can dynamically adjust resource allocation and processing stages based on real-time load and available system resources, balancing memory efficiency and processing speed. The system is optimized for both throughput and latency, carefully managing resource contention and memory usage.']

