In terms of performance optimization, the application is optimized for maintainability and readability by following Rust best practices, such as modular design, dependency injection, and type safety. It also includes comprehensive unit tests and integration tests to cover all critical paths, including successful queries, failed connections, parameter binding, and backend switching scenarios. End-to-end tests are also included to simulate real-world usage patterns and validate the application's robustness under load.

