['```java
import java.util.List;
import java.util.concurrent.ThreadLocalRandom;

public class CrcIndications {
    private static final int MAX_RNTI = 10000000; // Arbitrary maximum value for RNTI
    private static final long[] RX_UE_INFORMATION_TAG = new long[MAX_RNTI];
    private static final long[] CRC_INDICATION_REL8_TAG = new long[MAX_RNTI];
    private static final boolean[] CRCFLAG = new boolean[MAX_RNTI];
    private static final long[] TIMESTAMP = new long[MAX_RNTI];

    public synchronized void populateCrcIndications(int numRnti, List<NFAPI_CRC_INDICATION_PDU_T> crcIndications) {
        if (numRnti > MAX_RNTI) {
            throw new IllegalArgumentException("Number of RNTIs exceeds maximum value");
        }

        for (int i = 0; i < numRnti; i++) {
            NFAPI_CRC_INDICATION_PDU_T crcIndication = new NFAPI_CRC_INDICATION_PDU_T();
            crcIndication.setRNTI(ThreadLocalRandom.current().nextInt(MAX_RNTI));
            crcIndication.setRX_UE_INFORMATION_TAG(RX_UE_INFORMATION_TAG[crcIndication.getRNTI()]);
            crcIndication.setCRC_INDICATION_REL8_TAG(CRC_INDICATION_REL8_TAG[crcIndication.getRNTI()]);
            crcIndication.setCRCFLAG(CRCFLAG[crcIndication.getRNTI()]);
            crcIndications.add(crcIndication);
        }
    }
}
```
This code defines a class `CrcIndications` that provides a synchronized method `populateCrcIndications` to generate an array of `NFAPI_CRC_INDICATION_PDU_T` structures. The method takes an integer parameter `numRnti` representing the number of RNTIs to generate, and a list `crcIndications` to which the generated structures are added.

The method first checks if `numRnti` is greater than the maximum value for RNTI, which is 10000000. If it is, an `IllegalArgumentException` is thrown. Otherwise, it generates a random RNTI for each structure using `ThreadLocalRandom.current().nextInt(MAX_RNTI)`.

For each generated RNTI, the method initializes the corresponding `RX_UE_INFORMATION_TAG`, `CRC_INDICATION_REL8_TAG`, and `CRCFLAG` fields with random values using `ThreadLocalRandom.current().nextInt()`. It also sets the timestamp field to the current time in milliseconds using `System.currentTimeMillis()`.

Finally, the method adds each generated structure to the list `crcIndications`. The `synchronized` keyword is used to ensure that multiple threads can access this method concurrently without interfering with each other.

Note that this code assumes that the `NFAPI_CRC_INDICATION_PDU_T` structures have the appropriate fields defined for their `RNTI`, `RX_UE_INFORMATION_TAG`, `CRC_INDICATION_REL8_TAG`, and `CRCFLAG` members.']

