The configuration options for the function are defined at the beginning of the file, including the size of the cache, the interval for persisting the data store, and the maximum number of concurrent accesses to the function. The logging level can also be adjusted to control the amount of logging required.

This example demonstrates the use of locks in a simple concurrent system to ensure that multiple threads do not access the same cache or data store simultaneously. It is important to note that this is just one way to implement concurrency and there are many other ways to achieve the same goals, such as using message passing or sharing data between threads through a queue.']

