Note that the `Run` method uses a while loop to continuously check for new frames in the buffer and process them. This allows the manager to handle multiple incoming frames simultaneously without blocking other parts of the system. However, if the buffer becomes too large, it may become a bottleneck and affect performance. In this example, we use a fixed-size buffer that is preallocated to store a maximum number of frames. You can adjust this value based on your specific requirements.

