The constructor takes parameters for the number of PDUs to generate (`N`), an optional seed for random number generation, and configuration settings for external services, including a message queue provider and database connection strings. The `initialize()` function is used to initialize the internal state variables, including generating random PDUs using a Mersenne Twister algorithm and initializing external services. The `run()` function runs in a background thread and sends each generated PDU to message queue and database using external services. The `stop()` function stops the manager and cleans up any resources used.

The class also includes retry logic for external service failures with configurable backoff strategies, logging errors if all retries fail, and minimizing memory allocation overhead and maximizing throughput by using lock-free algorithms and data structures where appropriate. The `retryCount_` variable keeps track of the number of retries for each external service, and the `backoffStrategy_` variable specifies the backoff strategy (currently set to linear). The `logErrors_` variable determines whether or not to log errors if all retries fail.

The class also includes error handling for any exceptions that may occur during runtime.

